05:03:42.860 --> 05:03:49.668
we can use the bottleneck value to argument
the flow along the path. augmenting the flow

05:03:49.668 --> 05:03:55.229
simply means to update the flow values of
the edges along the augmenting path. Here

05:03:55.229 --> 05:04:01.238
you can see that I've increased the flow of
each edge along the augmenting path by exactly

05:04:01.238 --> 05:04:07.110
six units. However, we're not done augmenting
the flow, we not only need to increase the

05:04:07.110 --> 05:04:13.068
flow along the forward edges, but also decrease
the flow along the backwards edges, which

05:04:13.068 --> 05:04:18.860
are called residual edges, the residual edges
or the dotted edges going backwards in the

05:04:18.860 --> 05:04:26.498
reverse order of the augmenting path. The
logic behind having residual edges is to undo

05:04:26.498 --> 05:04:33.320
bad choices of augmenting paths which do not
lead to a maximum flow effectively, we don't

05:04:33.320 --> 05:04:40.030
know which are the best or even correct augmenting
paths to take. So this mechanism enables us

05:04:40.030 --> 05:04:45.048
to freely find any augmenting paths without
having to worry about whether or not we'll

05:04:45.048 --> 05:04:51.728
be able to achieve the maximum flow. It should
be mentioned that residual edges become valid

05:04:51.728 --> 05:04:58.280
edges to take when finding an augmenting path
in later iterations. So if we take a step

05:04:58.280 --> 05:05:05.668
back, you can think of every edge in the original
